  "notes": "# P1-01 bounded qualification \u2014 15 October 2026\n\nMeasured source is 559fafc4fb52e586606f5fdf471ce65f44c5cf58, production anchor 58e91dcef111bf02f773dcbfd1921d428cf75e34. The two unchanged original files passed 16/16 registered tests. Only those 16 tests populate this receipt. Separately, the generator checked 38 schemas and 75 direct parity fixtures; nine other A4 record/trust JSON files are outside that layout. Three private Node probe modes check literal vectors, one authorized receipt's unknown top-level member, and current publication bytes/markers. These are not additional registered tests or permanent regression coverage.\n\nThe closed root journal retains 21 command records, including these nonzero rows: {\"duplicates\": 1, \"dead-code\": 1, \"source-control\": 1}. Quality findings remain unwaived. The separate typed stripping control retains seven child records: [{\"phase\": \"baseline-receipt\", \"exit\": 0}, {\"phase\": \"baseline-schemas\", \"exit\": 0}, {\"phase\": \"mutant-compile\", \"exit\": 0}, {\"phase\": \"mutant-receipt\", \"exit\": 1}, {\"phase\": \"mutant-schemas\", \"exit\": 1}, {\"phase\": \"restored-receipt\", \"exit\": 0}, {\"phase\": \"restored-schemas\", \"exit\": 0}]. They repeat receipt/schema checks in a private physical copy, including compilation and two expected negative checks, without regeneration. Their actual restoration and failure attribution remain in the result, audit and outcome. Nested child records and their parent wrapper row are not separate top-level runs.\n\nThe v4 control required real TypeScript compilation to exit 0. It retained the exact known thin compiler kernel output (SHA-256 prefix 7960e3a), then restored the accepted kernel bytes (SHA-256 prefix 501cb876) before the probes. The receipt/schema checks exercise direct compiled contract modules with that kernel held constant. This is not a fresh full mutant build or proof of a mutated bundled-kernel route.\n\nThe earlier literal passthrough attempt remains halted and preserved. Its actual children exited 0, 0 and 2: real TypeScript compilation reported TS2339 before either mutant negative check or restoration. It is a failed control attempt, not a product failure or successful sensitivity proof. The later stripping control does not close the exact literal-passthrough specification criterion.\n\nRequired permanent tests/contracts files remain absent. Shape parity does not verify lifecycle semantics, provenance authority, trust admission or truth. Publication byte/HTML marker checks do not establish full HTML equivalence or deployed HTTP availability. Evidence exports omit a portable hash preimage. Full suite, coverage, Node24, hosted CI, release/pack, external identity, formal dependency acceptance and tracker Done remain unqualified. Shared A4/index ownership, paused work and pending transfers remain. Source, compiled, Pages, physical and failed-attempt indices stay private, unsplit hash references. Formal acceptance is false.\n\nThe ordinary staged whitespace check exited 2 with eight diagnostics in two byte-exact frozen artifacts: six diff-context trailing spaces and one blank EOF in the preparation diff, plus one blank EOF in the original successful build log. The raw result and exact-copy proof are retained under validation; no bytes were trimmed and no hook, freeze or quality policy was bypassed. Normal receipt and accepted-base freeze checks remain separate.\n"
